  "summary": "Unpacks a 6912-byte screen to $4000 from three streams (literals, masks, flags) whose offsets from the entry are in a header after the JR; a flag bit per 8 bytes says a mask byte follows, a mask bit per byte says repeat the previous byte or take a literal. Position independent: a POP HL; JP (HL) probe at $4000 finds its own address. The header's offsets and border byte differ per picture.",
